{"seq":37,"trial_id":"v04-cal-r3-2026-11/openclaw-opus-gbrain-told-live-rr-l3-mu-v04-dev/rr-09-l3-marrow-fieldworks-ticket-retired/r1","wall_ts":"2026-11-07T00:29:54.451Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-21T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"6d14741aea35121dddfcbcecf4d6a14ffc10ed36cf07aad951f710c9fb6a983e","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DV04CAL0002","text":"Hi Pree, here's what I can find on both.\n\n*Driver SMS prompt glitch on overflow lots: ticket #4412.* Moss's Central handoff digest from 2 Jan 2026 lists it as a minor glitch with the driver SMS prompt when combine trailers are staged on unpaved overflow lots. Hollis flagged it as open before Marrow Fieldworks changed hands on Mon 5 Jan 2026. The same note lists #4409, a recurring timeout on the Gatehouse Check-In report at Salina North (Bay 4 and the west grain-bin apron, during the 06:00 flatbed intake). I haven't seen any later update on #4412, so I can't tell you whether it's been closed.\n\n*West yard Door 2 double-booking: ticket #8841.* In #central-random on 13 Oct, Tobias said he'd checked the Plains depots. West yard Door 2 is still double-booking when flatbeds check in early at the kiosk, and he flagged it to support on #8841. This came up when Hollis asked him whether the webhook patch had fixed the tractor-bay alerts on \"Tobias's dealer account\". Nobody actually named Marrow Fieldworks there; I'm assuming it's the same account because of the January handoff. Worth checking with Tobias before you file it. I haven't seen a status update since.\n\nThere are no Marrow Fieldworks ticket, CRM or profile files in the shared drive I can see, so this all comes from that digest and the channel thread."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DV04CAL0002","ts":"1792591200.000129"}}
